--- /dev/null
+++ b/vendor/candle-core/PLERVO-PATCH.md
@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+# Candle ZIP compatibility patch
+
+Source: Hugging Face candle-core 0.9.2, crates.io, MIT OR Apache-2.0.
+The original LICENSE and source notices are retained. This patch changes the ZIP
+requirement from 7.2.0 to 9.0.4, adapts member-name decoding in npy.rs and pickle.rs,
+and adds a synthetic NPZ regression. The other 59 Rust library source files are
+byte-for-byte copies of the published crate. Upstream examples, tests, benches and
+their private build fixtures are omitted. Cargo.lock pins ZIP and its transitive
+package checksums.
+
+ZIP 9.0.4 includes fixes for RUSTSEC-2026-0367, RUSTSEC-2026-0368 and
+RUSTSEC-2026-0369. Newer Candle releases still depend on older ZIP majors and also
+introduce an unconditional tokenizers dependency; retaining 0.9.2 preserves the
+application's existing pure-Rust inference configuration.
+
+Candle's NPZ/PTH APIs read selected archive members into memory; the application
+must continue to avoid generic archive extraction into the filesystem. The package
+is a reviewed local compatibility patch, not an upstream release by Hugging Face.
+
+ZIP 9 returns decoded member names as Results. npy.rs and pickle.rs now
+propagate name-decoding errors and own successfully decoded names. No numerical
+code or archive extraction behavior is changed.
+
+A synthetic regression writes and reads an NPZ with a Unicode tensor name,
+checks exact float values through eager and lazy readers, and exercises PTH
+member discovery without filesystem archive extraction.
